<DocsPageTitle Path="Components/PropertyGrid">
    Blazorise PropertyGrid component
</DocsPageTitle>

<DocsPageLead>
    Display and edit related values in a compact two-column property inspector.
</DocsPageLead>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    Use <Code Tag>PropertyGrid</Code>, <Code Tag>PropertyGridGroup</Code>, and the individual editor components when the properties are known in Razor markup.
    Use <Code Tag>PropertyGridView</Code> when properties are described by a <Code>PropertyGridSchema</Code> and need to be generated dynamically.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    A schema is a snapshot of the values to render.
    Handle <Code>PropertyValueChanged</Code> to update the application model, then assign a new schema when the displayed values need to change.
    The built-in toolbar lets users search properties and switch between categorized and alphabetical views.
    Selecting a property displays its <Code>Description</Code> in the help panel.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    The property viewport scrolls independently when the component receives a constrained height, keeping the toolbar and help panel visible.
    Groups and property rows expose grid, row, gridcell, selection, and expansion semantics for assistive technologies.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageSubtitle>
    Examples
</DocsPageSubtitle>

